@page "/articles"
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@inject NavigationManager navigationManager

<div class="container">
    <div class="py-4 py-md-5" id="top"></div>

    @* MAT Tool *@
    <section class="card shadow-sm" id="matTool">
        <div class="card-body p-4">
            <h2 class="card-title">
                MAT Tool — Miscellaneous Administrative Tasks
            </h2>

            <p class="text-body-secondary">
                Visual Basic · SQL Server · Application Maintenance
            </p>

            <h3 class="h5 mt-4">Overview</h3>

            <p>
                I am the sole maintainer of a long-standing administrative
                application used by the service desk to carry out routine
                operational tasks, including adding users to various
                applications.
            </p>

            <h3 class="h5 mt-4">My Contribution</h3>

            <p>
                Over time, I have extended the application's functionality
                by adding new tabs and capabilities to support additional
                administrative tasks. This involves maintaining and
                modifying the existing Visual Basic code and SQL Server
                components.
            </p>

            <p class="mb-0">
                This work requires understanding an established codebase,
                assessing the impact of changes and maintaining the
                reliability of an application used in day-to-day operations.
            </p>

            <h3 class="h5 mt-4">Configurable Task Type Functionality</h3>

            <p class="mb-2">
                One of the enhancements I introduced was a configurable task type system, 
                allowing the Service Desk to carry out additional administrative tasks 
                through a consistent interface.
            </p>

            <p class="mb-2">
                Users can select from a list of predefined task types. Depending on the selection, 
                the application dynamically displays the relevant input fields, allowing users to enter 
                the required parameters and submit the task for processing.
            </p>

            <p class="mb-2">
                Each task type can define up to six parameters, with configurable labels stored in a SQL Server table. 
                Parameters can accept free-text input or populate dropdown lists using dedicated stored procedures.
            </p>

            <p class="mb-2">
                When a task is submitted, the application executes the associated SQL stored procedure. 
                Users can then view the outcome, including confirmation of successful completion or any error 
                or feedback messages.
            </p>

            <h3 class="h5 mt-4">Benefits</h3>

            <p class="mb-2">
                This enhancement introduced a flexible way to add new Service Desk tasks without requiring 
                changes to the application's existing code.
            </p>

            <p class="mb-0">
                New tasks can be made available by:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>
                    Writing a SQL stored procedure to perform the required operation.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Adding an entry to the task type configuration table.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Defining the required parameters and their labels.
                </li>
            </ul>

        </div>
    </section>

    @* Secondments *@
    <div class="py-2 mb-4" id="secondments"></div>

     @* Secondment 2023-2024 *@
    <section class="card shadow-sm mb-4">
            
        <div class="card-body p-4">
            <div class="row mb-3 pt-3">
                <h3 class="h3 card-title">Secondment 2023-2024</h3>
                <p class="mt-3">
                    I spent a day a week for about a year in 2023/2024 working with a development team as a developer.
                </p>
                <p>
                    I worked on various systems analysing and fixing issues. 
                </p>
                <p>
                    I had some substantial coding experience to the end of this time on a rewrite of an application in C#.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    @* Secondment 2018 *@
    <section class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body p-4">
            <div class="row mb-3 pt-3">
                <h3 class="card-title">Secondment 2018</h3>
                <p class="mt-3">
                    I spent 3 months with a development team in 2018 working on small development requirements.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    @* Daily work *@
    <section class="card shadow-sm mb-4" id="dailyWork">

        <div class="card-body p-4">
            <div class="row mb-3 pt-3">
                <h3 class="card-title">Daily work</h3>
                <p class="mt-3">
                    On a daily basis I interact with the code base in Azure DevOps. 
                </p>
                <p>
                    Many incidents require reading through code and debugging it to resolve issues.
                </p>
                <p>
                    On occasion I have the oPportunity to make small code changes which require going through 
                    the entire life cycle of a change from requirement specification to development, testing and deployment. 
                </p>
                <p>
                    It also required working closely with various dev teams organising environments and with 
                    the business to confirm the issue has been resolved.
                </p>

            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    @* Footer *@
    <footer class="mt-4 pt-4 pb-3">
        <div class="row mb-3">
            <div class="col-6">
                <button class="btn btn-primary" @onclick="() => ReturnButton()">Return to home</button>
            </div>
            <div class="col-6 mt-1">
                <a href="articles#top" class="link-secondary">
                    Back to top ↑
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </footer>
</div>

@code {

    private void ReturnButton() => navigationManager!.NavigateTo("/");

}
